===============================================================================
WHAT THIS LICENCE COVERS, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT
===============================================================================

The MIT grant above applies to the **source code in this repository**: everything
under `PrinceOfPersia/` and `Scripts/`, and the prose in `README.md` and
`ARCHITECTURE.md`. It is the author's own work, written from publicly available
reimplementations rather than from any original source.

It does **not** apply to the game itself. The artwork, music and sound effects
are Ubisoft's, and no one but Ubisoft can license them. That includes:

  PrinceOfPersia/Sources/PoPCore/Resources/    artwork, music, sound, level data
  build/Prince of Persia.app/                  a compiled copy of the above
  screenshots/, appicon.png                    screenshots of it, and an icon derived from it

Those files are included because a port of a game is meaningless without the game's
own assets. They are here for **preservation, study and demonstration**, they are not
for sale, and they are not covered by the MIT grant — which is to say that nothing
in this licence should be read as granting rights in Prince of Persia.

See `ASSETS.md` for where each file came from and what the position is.

If you are Ubisoft and you would like this repository taken down, open an issue and
it will be removed.
